Options
booleanOption _ a3.bool;
booleanOption _ a4.bool;
booleanOption _ a5.bool;
booleanOption _ a6.bool;
Change for this round: add multi-part names.
	A name of the form a.b.c is stored, for the moment, in the name 
Commands

[viewer: ViewerClasses.Viewer, instanceData: REF ANY, classData: REF ANY, key: REF ANY]
$TiogaContents => { -- to split it apart!!
contents, formatting: Rope.ROPE;
dataLen, count: INT;
[dataLen, count, contents] _ TiogaIO.ToRope[tdd.text];
formatting _ Rope.Substr[base: contents, start: dataLen, len: count-dataLen];
contents _ Rope.Substr[base: contents, start: 0, len: dataLen];
data _ NEW[ViewerTools.TiogaContentsRec _ [contents, formatting]];
};
node: #NIL means that the node's text is to be used as the definition.  FALSE means that the definition comes from rawDef, comprising everything up to but not including the next line delimiter.
In future
WHILE TRUE DO -- Collect compound name.
token.length _ 0;
token _ defStream.GetToken[IO.TokenProc, token].token;
name _ LowerCaseRope[Rope.FromRefText[token]];
newCommand _ CONS[[$command, name], newCommand];
IF tail = NIL THEN tail _ newCommand;
IF defStream.EndOf[] OR defStream.PeekChar[] # '. THEN EXIT;

For Now
[] _ defStream.SkipWhitespace[FALSE]; -- eats up placeholder brackets, etc.
Return value is always FALSE, by agreement.
Also, procData is never used, by current agreement.
For now, ignore dictAtom and keyDeterminesDict.
Try to accommodate non-Tioga AKA definitions.
Evaluate the alias
Substitute indices for formal parameters
Bind actual parameters to formal parameters
Utilities

if old is not found in base, then value = base.
if allOccurrences THEN substitute for each occurrence of old, otherwise only for first.
RETURN[Rope.MakeRope[base: r, size: r.Length[], fetch: LCFetch]]};

